    <fr:title text="Preimage">Preimage</fr:title>
    <fr:taxon>Definition</fr:taxon>
  </fr:frontmatter>
  <fr:mainmatter>
    <html:p>
    Let <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[f:X\to  Y]]></fr:tex> be a function and <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[y\in  Y]]></fr:tex>.
    The <html:strong>preimage</html:strong> of <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[y]]></fr:tex> under <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[f]]></fr:tex>, denoted by <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[f^{-1}(y)]]></fr:tex>, is the subset
    of <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[X]]></fr:tex> defined by
    <fr:tex display="block"><![CDATA[
        f^{-1}(y) = \set {x \in  X \mid  f(x) = y}
    ]]></fr:tex>
    For a subset <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[B \subseteq  Y]]></fr:tex>, the <html:strong>preimage</html:strong> of <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[B]]></fr:tex> under <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[f]]></fr:tex> is the subset
    of <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[X]]></fr:tex> defined by
    <fr:tex display="block"><![CDATA[
        f^{-1}(B) = \set {x \in  X \mid  f(x) \in  B}
    ]]></fr:tex></html:p>
  </fr:mainmatter>
